    {
      "decision_template": "Folded cascode topology (W_CP={w_cp}um L_CP={l_cp}um, W_CN={w_cn}um L_CN={l_cn}um)",
      "reason": "By folding the input pair current into PMOS cascode devices rather than telescoping, the output swing is decoupled from the input common-mode range. Both PMOS and NMOS cascode devices increase Rout to gm_casc × ro², boosting voltage gain by ~40dB over a simple differential pair.",
      "tradeoffs": "Requires four bias voltages (VBP, VBN, VCBP, VCBN). Higher power than telescopic. Dominant pole set by output capacitance.",
      "alternatives": ["Telescopic OTA (lower power)", "Two-stage Miller OTA (higher swing)"],
      "references": ["Razavi Analog CMOS Ch.9", "Folded Cascode OTA Design Guide - Tsividis"],
